#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:508
msgid ""
"List of `APT packages`_ to install. Our build servers run various Ubuntu LTS"
" versions with the default set of package repositories installed. We don't "
"currently support PPA's or other custom repositories."
msgstr ""
"要安装的 `APT packages`_ 列表。我们的构建服务器运行各种 Ubuntu LTS 版本，安装了默认的包仓库。目前不支持 PPA "
"或其他自定义仓库。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:528
msgid ""
"When possible avoid installing Python packages using apt (``python3-numpy`` "
"for example), :doc:`use pip or conda instead </guides/reproducible-builds>`."
msgstr ""
"尽可能避免使用 apt 安装 Python 包（例如 ``python3-numpy``），请 :doc:`改用 pip 或 conda "
"</guides/reproducible-builds>`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:533
msgid ""
"Currently, it's not possible to use this option when using :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:build.commands`."
msgstr "使用 :ref:`config-file/v2:build.commands` 时，目前无法使用此选项。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:537
msgid "build.jobs"
msgstr "build.jobs"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:539
msgid ""
"Commands to be run before or after a Read the Docs :term:`pre-defined build "
"jobs`, or to override a specific job. This allows you to run custom commands"
" at a particular moment in the build process. See :doc:`/build-"
"customization` for more details."
msgstr ""
"在 Read the Docs :term:`pre-defined build jobs` "
"之前或之后运行命令，或覆盖特定任务。这允许你在构建过程的特定时刻运行自定义命令。详情请参阅 :doc:`/build-customization`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:561
msgid ""
"Each build step consists of a list of commands to be executed. ``build.os`` "
"and ``build.tools`` are also required to use ``build.jobs``."
msgstr "每个构建步骤包含一组要执行的命令。使用 ``build.jobs`` 也需要 ``build.os`` 和 ``build.tools``。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:566
msgid ""
"If the :ref:`config-file/v2:sphinx` or  :ref:`config-file/v2:mkdocs` keys "
"are present in the configuration file, the default steps for each tool will "
"be executed for the ``create_environment``, ``install``, and ``build`` "
"steps. You can override any of these steps, but be aware that some steps may"
" depend on others, for example, the default ``install`` and ``build`` steps "
"depend on the ``create_environment`` step creating the Python virtual "
"environment in a specific directory."
msgstr ""
"如果配置文件中包含 :ref:`config-file/v2:sphinx` 或 :ref:`config-file/v2:mkdocs` 键，则会为 "
"``create_environment``、``install`` 和 ``build`` "
"步骤执行各工具的默认步骤。你可以覆盖这些步骤中的任意一个，但请注意某些步骤可能依赖其他步骤，例如默认的 ``install`` 和 ``build`` "
"步骤依赖 ``create_environment`` 步骤在特定目录创建 Python 虚拟环境。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:571
msgid ""
"If neither of the ``sphinx`` or ``mkdocs`` keys are present in the "
"configuration file, only the specified ``build.tools`` and "
"``build.apt_packages`` will be installed, you will in charge of generating "
"the documentation in the :ref:`$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT <build-"
"customization:where to put files>` directory."
msgstr ""
"如果配置文件中既没有 ``sphinx`` 也没有 ``mkdocs`` 键，则仅安装指定的 ``build.tools`` 和 "
"``build.apt_packages``，你需要负责在 :ref:`$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT <build-"
"customization:where to put files>` 目录中生成文档。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst
msgid "Allowed keys"
msgstr "允许的键"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:576
msgid ""
"``post_checkout``, ``pre_system_dependencies``, "
"``post_system_dependencies``, ``pre_create_environment``, "
"``create_environment``, ``post_create_environment``, ``pre_install``, "
"``post_install``, ``pre_build``, ``build``, ``post_build``"
msgstr ""
"``post_checkout``, ``pre_system_dependencies``, "
"``post_system_dependencies``, ``pre_create_environment``, "
"``create_environment``, ``post_create_environment``, ``pre_install``, "
"``post_install``, ``pre_build``, ``build``, ``post_build``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:580
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:619
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:877
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``{}``"
msgstr "``{}``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:583
msgid "build.jobs.build"
msgstr "build.jobs.build"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:585
msgid ""
"Commands to override the default build process. When running builds from "
"pull requests, only the ``html`` step will be executed."
msgstr "覆盖默认构建过程的命令。运行 Pull Request 构建时，仅执行 ``html`` 步骤。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:617
msgid "``html``, ``pdf``, ``epub``, ``htmlzip``"
msgstr "``html``, ``pdf``, ``epub``, ``htmlzip``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:623
msgid ""
"If any of the ``pdf``, ``epub``, or ``htmlzip`` steps are overridden, they "
"should be included in the :ref:`config-file/v2:formats` list."
msgstr ""
"如果覆盖了 ``pdf``、``epub`` 或 ``htmlzip`` 步骤，应将它们包含在 :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:formats` 列表中。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:628
msgid ""
"For each format, you need to generate their output in the "
":ref:`$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT <build-customization:where to put files>` "
"directory."
msgstr ""
"每种格式都需要在 :ref:`$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT <build-customization:where to put files>`"
" 目录中生成输出。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:631
msgid "build.commands"
msgstr "build.commands"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:633
msgid ""
"Specify a list of commands that Read the Docs will run on the build process."
" When ``build.commands`` is used, none of the :term:`pre-defined build jobs`"
" will be executed."
msgstr ""
"指定 Read the Docs 在构建过程中运行的命令列表。使用 ``build.commands`` 时，不会执行任何 :term:`pre-"
"defined build jobs`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:648
msgid "But we recommend using :ref:`config-file/v2:build.jobs` instead:"
msgstr "但我们建议改用 :ref:`config-file/v2:build.jobs`："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:665
msgid ""
"``build.jobs`` offers the same functionality as ``build.commands``, but in a"
" more structured way that allows you to define different commands for each "
"format, while also supporting installing system dependencies via "
"``build.apt_packages``. See :doc:`/build-customization` for more details."
msgstr ""
"``build.jobs`` 提供与 ``build.commands`` 相同的功能，但以更结构化的方式，允许为每种格式定义不同的命令，同时支持通过 "
"``build.apt_packages`` 安装系统依赖。详情请参阅 :doc:`/build-customization`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:672
msgid ""
"``build.os`` and ``build.tools`` are also required when using "
"``build.commands``."
msgstr "使用 ``build.commands`` 时也需要 ``build.os`` 和 ``build.tools``。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:676
msgid ""
"All items in the ``build.commands`` array are executed in a clean shell "
"environment, i.e. environment changes do not persist and the working "
"directory always start from the git repo."
msgstr "``build.commands`` 数组中的所有项目都在干净的 shell 环境中执行，即环境变化不持久化，工作目录始终从 git 仓库开始。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:685
msgid "sphinx"
msgstr "sphinx"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:687
msgid "Configuration for Sphinx documentation."
msgstr "Sphinx 文档的配置。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:699
msgid ""
"If you want to pin Sphinx to a specific version, use a ``requirements.txt`` "
"or ``environment.yml`` file (see :ref:`config-file/v2:requirements file` and"
"  :ref:`config-file/v2:conda.environment`). If you are using a metadata file"
" to describe code dependencies like ``setup.py``, ``pyproject.toml``, or "
"similar, you can use the ``extra_requirements`` option (see :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:packages`). This also allows you to override :ref:`the default "
"pinning done by Read the Docs if your project was created before October "
"2020 <build-default-versions:external dependencies>`."
msgstr ""
"如果要将 Sphinx 固定到特定版本，请使用 ``requirements.txt`` 或 ``environment.yml`` 文件（参见 "
":ref:`config-file/v2:requirements file` 和 :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:conda.environment`）。如果你使用 ``setup.py``、``pyproject.toml`` "
"等元数据文件描述代码依赖，可以使用 ``extra_requirements`` 选项（参见 :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:packages`）。这也允许你覆盖 :ref:`Read the Docs 为 2020 年 10 月前创建的项目所做的默认固定 "
"<build-default-versions:external dependencies>`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:710
msgid "sphinx.builder"
msgstr "sphinx.builder"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:712
msgid "The builder type for the Sphinx documentation."
msgstr "Sphinx 文档的构建器类型。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:715
msgid "``html``, ``dirhtml``, ``singlehtml``"
msgstr "``html``, ``dirhtml``, ``singlehtml``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:716
msgid "``html``"
msgstr "``html``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:719
msgid ""
"The ``htmldir`` builder option was renamed to ``dirhtml`` to use the same "
"name as sphinx. Configurations using the old name will continue working."
msgstr "``htmldir`` 构建器选项已重命名为 ``dirhtml``，以与 sphinx 使用相同名称。使用旧名称的配置将继续工作。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:723
msgid "sphinx.configuration"
msgstr "sphinx.configuration"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:725
msgid "The path to the ``conf.py`` file, relative to the root of the project."
msgstr "``conf.py`` 文件的路径，相对于项目根目录。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:731
msgid "sphinx.fail_on_warning"
msgstr "sphinx.fail_on_warning"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:733
msgid ""
"Turn warnings into errors (:option:`-W <sphinx:sphinx-build.-W>` and :option"
":`--keep-going <sphinx:sphinx-build.--keep-going>` options). This means the "
"build fails if there is a warning and exits with exit status 1."
msgstr ""
"将警告转为错误（:option:`-W <sphinx:sphinx-build.-W>` 和 :option:`--keep-going "
"<sphinx:sphinx-build.--keep-going>` 选项）。这意味着构建若有警告即失败，退出状态为 1。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:737
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:778
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:848
msgid "``bool``"
msgstr "``bool``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:741
msgid "mkdocs"
msgstr "mkdocs"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:743
msgid "Configuration for MkDocs documentation."
msgstr "MkDocs 文档的配置。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:754
msgid ""
"If you want to pin MkDocs to a specific version, use a ``requirements.txt`` "
"or ``environment.yml`` file (see :ref:`config-file/v2:requirements file` and"
"  :ref:`config-file/v2:conda.environment`). If you are using a metadata file"
" to describe code dependencies like ``setup.py``, ``pyproject.toml``, or "
"similar, you can use the ``extra_requirements`` option (see :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:packages`). This also allows you to override :ref:`the default "
"pinning done by Read the Docs if your project was created before March 2021 "
"<build-default-versions:external dependencies>`."
msgstr ""
"如果要将 MkDocs 固定到特定版本，请使用 ``requirements.txt`` 或 ``environment.yml`` 文件（参见 "
":ref:`config-file/v2:requirements file` 和 :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:conda.environment`）。如果你使用 ``setup.py``、``pyproject.toml`` "
"等元数据文件描述代码依赖，可使用 ``extra_requirements`` 选项（参见 :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:packages`）。这也允许你覆盖 :ref:`Read the Docs 为 2021 年 3 月前创建的项目所做的默认固定 "
"<build-default-versions:external dependencies>`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:765
msgid "mkdocs.configuration"
msgstr "mkdocs.configuration"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:767
msgid "The path to the ``mkdocs.yml`` file, relative to the root of the project."
msgstr "``mkdocs.yml`` 文件的路径，相对于项目根目录。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:773
msgid "mkdocs.fail_on_warning"
msgstr "mkdocs.fail_on_warning"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:775
msgid ""
"`Turn warnings into errors <https://www.mkdocs.org/user-"
"guide/configuration/#strict>`__. This means that the build stops at the "
"first warning and exits with exit status 1."
msgstr ""
"`将警告转为错误 <https://www.mkdocs.org/user-"
"guide/configuration/#strict>`__。这意味着构建在第一个警告时停止，退出状态为 1。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:782
msgid "submodules"
msgstr "submodules"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:784
msgid "VCS submodules configuration."
msgstr "VCS 子模块配置。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:788
msgid "Only Git is supported at the moment."
msgstr "目前仅支持 Git。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:792
msgid ""
"You can't use ``include`` and ``exclude`` settings for submodules at the "
"same time."
msgstr "不能同时对子模块使用 ``include`` 和 ``exclude`` 设置。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:805
msgid "submodules.include"
msgstr "submodules.include"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:807
msgid "List of submodules to be included."
msgstr "要包含的子模块列表。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:814
msgid "You can use the ``all`` keyword to include all submodules."
msgstr "可使用 ``all`` 关键字包含所有子模块。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:824
msgid "submodules.exclude"
msgstr "submodules.exclude"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:826
msgid "List of submodules to be excluded."
msgstr "要排除的子模块列表。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:833
msgid ""
"You can use the ``all`` keyword to exclude all submodules. This is the same "
"as ``include: []``."
msgstr "可使用 ``all`` 关键字排除所有子模块。这等同于 ``include: []``。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:844
msgid "submodules.recursive"
msgstr "submodules.recursive"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:846
msgid "Do a recursive clone of the submodules."
msgstr "递归克隆子模块。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:853
msgid "This is ignored if there aren't submodules to clone."
msgstr "如果没有要克隆的子模块，此项将被忽略。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:856
msgid "search"
msgstr "search"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:858
msgid "Settings for more control over :doc:`/server-side-search/index`."
msgstr "用于更精细控制 :doc:`/server-side-search/index` 的设置。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:872
msgid "search.ranking"
msgstr "search.ranking"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:874
msgid "Set a custom search rank over pages matching a pattern."
msgstr "为匹配模式的页面设置自定义搜索排名。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:876
msgid "``map`` of patterns to ranks"
msgstr "模式到排名的 ``map``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:879
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:930
msgid ""
"Patterns are matched against the relative paths of the HTML files produced "
"by the build, you should try to match ``index.html``, not "
"``docs/index.rst``, nor ``/en/latest/index.html``. Patterns can include one "
"or more of the following special characters:"
msgstr ""
"模式与构建生成的 HTML 文件的相对路径匹配，应尝试匹配 ``index.html``，而非 ``docs/index.rst`` 或 "
"``/en/latest/index.html``。模式可包含以下一个或多个特殊字符："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:883
msgid "``*`` matches everything, including slashes."
msgstr "``*`` 匹配所有内容，包括斜杠。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:884
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:935
msgid "``?`` matches any single character."
msgstr "``?`` 匹配任意单个字符。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:885
#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:936
msgid "``[seq]`` matches any character in ``seq``."
msgstr "``[seq]`` 匹配 ``seq`` 中的任意字符。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:887
msgid ""
"The rank can be an integer number between -10 and 10 (inclusive). Pages with"
" a rank closer to -10 will appear further down the list of results, and "
"pages with a rank closer to 10 will appear higher in the list of results. "
"Note that 0 means *normal rank*, not *no rank*."
msgstr ""
"排名可以是 -10 到 10 之间的整数（含边界）。排名越接近 -10 的页面在结果中越靠后，越接近 10 的越靠前。注意 0 表示*正常排名*，而非*"
" 无排名*。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:892
msgid ""
"If you are looking to completely ignore a page, check :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:search.ignore`."
msgstr "如果想完全忽略某页面，请参阅 :ref:`config-file/v2:search.ignore`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:914
msgid "The final rank will be the last pattern to match the page."
msgstr "最终排名将取匹配该页面的最后一个模式。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:918
msgid ""
"Is better to decrease the rank of pages you want to deprecate, rather than "
"increasing the rank of the other pages."
msgstr "最好降低想废弃页面的排名，而不是提高其他页面的排名。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:922
msgid "search.ignore"
msgstr "search.ignore"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:924
msgid ""
"List of paths to ignore and exclude from the search index. Paths matched "
"will not be included in search results."
msgstr "要忽略并从搜索索引中排除的路径列表。匹配的路径不会包含在搜索结果中。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:927
msgid "``list`` of patterns"
msgstr "模式的 ``list``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:928
msgid "``['search.html', 'search/index.html', '404.html', '404/index.html']``"
msgstr "``['search.html', 'search/index.html', '404.html', '404/index.html']``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:934
msgid "``*`` matches everything (including slashes)."
msgstr "``*`` 匹配所有内容（包括斜杠）。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:973
msgid ""
"Since Read the Docs fallbacks to the original search engine when no results "
"are found, you may still see search results from ignored pages."
msgstr "由于 Read the Docs 在未找到结果时会回退到原始搜索引擎，你可能仍会看到来自被忽略页面的搜索结果。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:977
msgid "Schema"
msgstr "Schema"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/config-file/v2.rst:979
msgid ""
"You can see the complete schema `here "
"<https://github.com/readthedocs/readthedocs.org/blob/main/readthedocs/rtd_tests/fixtures/spec/v2/schema.json>`_."
" This schema is available at `Schema Store`_, use it with your favorite "
"editor for validation and autocompletion."
msgstr ""
"你可以 `在此 "
"<https://github.com/readthedocs/readthedocs.org/blob/main/readthedocs/rtd_tests/fixtures/spec/v2/schema.json>`_"
" 查看完整 schema。该 schema 可在 `Schema Store`_ 获取，可配合你常用的编辑器用于验证和自动补全。"

